quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  40,50,They will say: ‘Did your messengers not used to bring you clear proofs?’ They will say: ‘Yes (they did).’ Then they (i.e. the keepers) will say: ‘Now pray (yourselves).’ But the supplications of the disbelievers will (always) be in vain.
  40,51,"Indeed, We support Our messengers and the believers (both) in this worldly life and on the Day when the witnesses will arise (for testimony),"
  40,52,"the Day when the excuses of the wrongdoers will not benefit them. The curse will lie on them, and for them will be the evil abode (of Hell)."
  40,53,"And certainly We gave Musa (Moses) guidance, and made the Children of Israel inherit the Book,"
  40,54,as a guide and a reminder for the possessors of wisdom.
  40,55,So be patient (O Prophet)! Allah’s promise is indeed true. And seek (Allah’s) forgiveness for the sins of your (community).* And glorify the praise of your Lord (every) morning and evening.
  40,56,"Surely, those who dispute the revelations of Allah without any authority that has come to them have nothing in their hearts except greed for greatness, which they will never attain. So, keep seeking refuge with Allah. Indeed, He is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing."
  40,57,"Surely, the creation of the heavens and the earth is far greater than the creation of humankind, but most people do not know."
  40,58,"The blind and the seeing cannot be equal; neither are those who believe and perform righteous deeds and those who commit evil. Yet, seldom do you accept advice."
